LINT                   GROUP        LEVEL  SUMMARY
shadows-builtin        suspicious   warn   a parameter or local binding shadows a built-in
deprecated-private     deprecated   warn   a library's bare top-level function (write it h:)
unknown-lint           suspicious   warn   a `# lint:` directive names no lint, group or level
unused-binding         suspicious   warn   a lambda parameter or local binding that is never used
redundant-lambda       complexity   warn   a lambda that only passes its arguments to a named function
missing-bang           style        warn   a function that calls an effect but has no `!` in its name
needless-bang          pedantic     allow  a `!` function that calls no effect
int-condition          suspicious   warn   a guard whose condition is an Int (a count), not a truth
function-name-case     pedantic     allow  a function named UpperCamel (functions are lowerCamel)
mutable-constant       style        warn   a mutable variable named like a constant (UpperCamel)
upper-case-name        pedantic     allow  a variable named in all capitals
needless-raw-hashes    style        warn   a raw string with more `#` than it needs
needless-raw-string    pedantic     allow  a raw string with no backslash, quote or newline (plain is the same)
escapes-could-be-raw   pedantic     allow  a string with several `\"` or `\\` escapes (clearer raw)
string-holds-directive suspicious   warn   a line inside a string that reads as a `# lint:` directive
